			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				129,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Project): Wire full editor IPC pipeline for decorations, text edits, selections, and hierarchy\n\nAdvance 8 element submodules in a coordinated update that completes the editor IPC round-trip from extension host to native backend to editor UI, enabling real-world extensions to manipulate text editors, decorations, and call/type hierarchy panels.\n\n**Cocoon** backfills critical VS Code API shims discovered through integration testing: extension exports resolution (`getExtension(id).exports`), call/type hierarchy prepare entry points, live `workspace.textDocuments` tracking via `$acceptModelAdded`/`$acceptModelRemoved`, `document.willSave` listener dispatch with edit collection, and a robust `activeTextEditor` stub supporting `setDecorations`, `edit`, `insertSnippet`, `revealRange`, and live selection tracking.\n\n**Common** extends the IPC event surface in SkyEvent.rs with five new URIs (`DecorationSetRanges`, `EditorApplyTextEdits`, `EditorSelectionChanged`, `EditorActiveChanged`, `EditorRevealRange`) and adds `PrepareCallHierarchy`/`PrepareTypeHierarchy` to the LanguageFeatureProviderRegistry trait, completing the hierarchy provider lifecycle defined by the VS Code LanguageFeatureRequest contract.\n\n**Mountain** implements the full gRPC+LSP pipeline for hierarchy prepare in new `PerformCallHierarchy`/`PerformTypeHierarchy` provider modules, bridges `window.setTextEditorDecorations` via a channel-drain batching mechanism (16 ms frame-aligned aggregation), and wires `window.applyTextEdits`/`window.revealRange` through to Sky events. A new `document.willSave` fire event grants extension listeners a 1.5-second grace window before disk write. Two new `mountain_ipc_invoke` handlers (`sky:editor:selectionChanged`, `sky:editor:activeChanged`) forward editor state changes from Sky to Cocoon.\n\n**Sky** registers four IPC bridge handlers matching editors by URI or filename segment: decoration range application via `ICodeEditorService`, text edit execution with dual-range-format normalization, reveal range delegation with the five standard strategies, and active editor/selection change subscription pushing state up to Mountain.\n\n**Wind** adds the five new Sky IPC event constants to `Source/IPC/SkyEvent.ts` while purging over 400 zero-byte generated stub files (`I*Upstream.ts`, `CommandCatalog.ts`, `ServiceCatalog.ts`, `*BridgeShapeGenerated.ts`).\n\n**Air** applies consistent import ordering and single-expression formatting across 4 subsystems. **Output** removes 160+ stale zero-byte build artifacts. **Grove** syncs the Rust documentation submodule. **Echo** advances to a clean commit.\n\nThis completes the editor IPC round-trip for text editor manipulation and call/type hierarchy, enabling extensions that depend on `window.activeTextEditor`, `editor.edit()`, `setDecorations`, `revealRange`, hierarchy providers, and format-on-save listeners to function correctly.",
			"SHA": "6f099a0735770518cac2a3476158965f14b899dd"
		}
